///
/// # Implementation sketch
/// The function swaps elements symmetrically around the center of the prefix:
/// for `i` in `0..k/2`, swap `s[i]` with `s[k-1-i]`.
/// No iteration over the suffix `k..s.len()` is needed.
///
/// # Verification
/// The loop invariant ensures that after each iteration, the partially reversed prefix
/// and the untouched suffix satisfy the specification relative to the initial state.
